The Trump administration’s assault on voting rights is a part of their broader attack on the progress made during the civil rights era.

Whether it is firing top generals based on the color of their skin, trying to rewrite history at the Smithsonian, suing our universities who want a diverse student body, or trying to suppress the vote, it is the same old story of bigotry and discrimination.

@naacpcahi has a long history of fighting for racial injustice and I was proud to honor this year’s awardees at their State Convention.

National Park workers at Yosemite maintain one of the most popular parks in the country – and they’re being devastated by this administration. 

First, many great staff members were DOGED. Now, many who remain face drastic pay cuts. 

@SenAlexPadilla and I are demanding @Interior reverse course. Our national parks do not take care of themselves. Their staff need our support.
